<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — Redd XF" description="How redd.in handles your data." canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/">
<main class="page-privacy">
<article class="article-content" style="max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;padding:2rem 1.25rem;">
<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p><em>Last updated: 12 October 2026</em></p>

<p>This policy explains how redd.in ("we", "us") handles information when you visit this website.</p>

<h2>What we collect</h2>
<p>We use privacy-respecting, cookieless analytics (PostHog, EU-hosted) to understand aggregate site usage — pages visited, referrers, and device type. No cookies are set for advertising, and we do not sell or share personal data with third parties.</p>

<h2>Third-party services</h2>
<p>This site loads fonts and icons from public CDNs. Embedded content (such as videos) may be served by third parties who set their own cookies under their own policies.</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>Under GDPR, you may request access to, correction of, or deletion of any personal data we hold about you. We keep no user accounts and minimal logs, so in practice there is very little to request — but if you'd like to exercise these rights, contact us and we will respond promptly.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:xf@redd.in">xf@redd.in</a>.</p>
</article>
</main>
</BaseLayout>